    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7070" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cătasta</span></b> , ae, f.
		
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατάστασις</span>
		 (postAug.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a scaffold</i>, <i>stage</i>, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>On which slaves were exposed for sale</i>, <i><span class="en">Tib. 2, 3,
				60</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Pers. 6, 77</span></i> Schol.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 35,
				18, 58, § 200</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Gram.
			13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 2, 1,
			72</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>For the public burning</i> (<i>of
				criminals</i>, <i>martyrs</i>, etc.), Prud.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 1, 56; 2, 399
			al.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>For delivering a lecture</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Rutil. 1, 393</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Cypr. Ep. 28</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
